          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "રાજા — rājā — \"a king\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "જૂના વખતમાં અહીં એક દયાળુ રાજા રહેતો હતો. jūnā vakhatmā̃ ahī̃ ek dayāḷu rājā raheto hato. Long ago a kind king lived here."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "રાજા (rājā) is inherited from Sanskrit rājan, \"a chieftain, a king\" (CDIAL 10679). It ends in -ā but does not change like છોકરો: રાજાનું ઘર, the king's house."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
